<!--CLI Capability — ParseArgs
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.capability.ParseArgs-->
<clicap:ParseArgs xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    core:Capability
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Parse process.argv slice into ParsedArgs
  </is>
  <documentation>
    # Parse process.argv slice into ParsedArgs
    
    CLI9: first non-flag token is command.
    
    Flags: --out, --src, --libraries (comma-split), --include (comma-split),
    --all, --per-package, --verbose, --json, --force, --limit, --depth,
    --origin and --relation (graph uses/used-by/neighbors, comma-split),
    --library (transform apply path to the target Library.bml; distinct
    from --libraries), --parameters (transform apply JSON value),
    --parameter-mappings (transform apply JSON array of ParameterMapping
    objects), --baseType and --is (new),
    --help / -h (print help page, exit 0). The token help as command or graph subcommand is the same.
    Root help is clidocumentation:Help. Command help is the Printed help section of that command documentation.
    Error paths print short USAGE, not the help page.
    
    Positional: validate=file; compile=target or file+target; search=query
    tokens or subcommand index; scan=package|type then selector tokens; graph=subcommand then args;
    inspect=FQN; transform=subcommand then args (apply=execution FQN); new=FQN.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="cliapi:ParsedArgs" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clidocumentation:Help" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
  <properties>
    <argv type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        Arguments after node and script path. (required)
      </documentation>
    </argv>
    <result type="cliapi:ParsedArgs">
      <documentation>
        Parsed arguments. (required)
      </documentation>
    </result>
  </properties>
</clicap:ParseArgs>
